{"page":720,"blocks":[{"x":0.04849,"y":0.05257,"w":0.36457,"h":0.01535,"fs":0.01535,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"706 Chapter 12: Vectors and the Geometry of Space"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.093,"w":0.23936,"h":0.01375,"fs":0.01375,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Distance and Spheres in Space"},{"x":0.20448,"y":0.10921,"w":0.06614,"h":0.01216,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"P2(x2, y2, z2)"},{"x":0.11776,"y":0.10922,"w":0.06615,"h":0.01215,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"P1(x1, y1, z1)"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.11764,"w":0.58896,"h":0.01281,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"The formula for the distance between two points in the xy-plane extends to points in space."},{"x":0.35359,"y":0.16527,"w":0.35329,"h":0.01445,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"The Distance Between P1(x1, y1, z1) and P2(x2, y2, z2)"},{"x":0.4579,"y":0.17536,"w":0.32223,"h":0.02776,"fs":0.01353,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"0 P1P20 = 2(x2 - x1)2 + (y2 - y1)2 + (z2 - z1)2"},{"x":0.2042,"y":0.20175,"w":0.06124,"h":0.01215,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"B(x2, y2, z1)"},{"x":0.11667,"y":0.21337,"w":0.06123,"h":0.01215,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"A(x2, y1, z1)"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.23659,"w":0.59303,"h":0.03077,"fs":0.01311,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"Proof We construct a rectangular box with faces parallel to the coordinate planes and the points P1 and P2 at opposite corners of the box (Figure 12.5). If A(x2, y1, z1) and"},{"x":0.04849,"y":0.25852,"w":0.22817,"h":0.05969,"fs":0.01151,"n":5,"k":1,"t":"FIGURE 12.5 We find the distance between P1 and P2 by applying the Pythagorean theorem to the right triangles P1AB and P1BP2."},{"x":0.32424,"y":0.26839,"w":0.59198,"h":0.02967,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"B(x2, y2, z1) are the vertices of the box indicated in the figure, then the three box edges P1A, AB, and BP2 have lengths"},{"x":0.40355,"y":0.29367,"w":0.43094,"h":0.02776,"fs":0.01353,"n":3,"k":0,"t":"0 P1A0 = 0 x2 - x10 , 0 AB0 = 0 y2 - y10 , 0 BP20 = 0 z2 - z10 ."},{"x":0.32333,"y":0.32977,"w":0.58902,"h":0.02815,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"Because triangles P1BP2 and P1AB are both right-angled, two applications of the Pythago- rean theorem give"},{"x":0.40358,"y":0.35506,"w":0.43089,"h":0.02741,"fs":0.01353,"n":3,"k":0,"t":"0 P1P20 2 = 0 P1B0 2 + 0 BP20 2 and 0 P1B0 2 = 0 P1A0 2 + 0 AB0 2"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.39118,"w":0.13676,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"(see Figure 12.5). So"},{"x":0.40839,"y":0.4011,"w":0.1737,"h":0.02741,"fs":0.01353,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"0 P1P20 2 = 0 P1B0 2 + 0 BP20 2"},{"x":0.45843,"y":0.42029,"w":0.34819,"h":0.02741,"fs":0.01353,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"= 0 P1A0 2 + 0 AB0 2 + 0 BP20 2 Substitute"},{"x":0.45843,"y":0.42865,"w":0.43579,"h":0.03858,"fs":0.01353,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"0 P1B0 2 = 0 P1A0 2 + 0 AB0 2. = 0 x2 - x10 2 + 0 y2 - y10 2 + 0 z2 - z10 2"},{"x":0.45843,"y":0.46659,"w":0.2672,"h":0.01982,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"= (x2 - x1)2 + (y2 - y1)2 + (z2 - z1)2 ."},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.49477,"w":0.06449,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Therefore"},{"x":0.45518,"y":0.50469,"w":0.32767,"h":0.02776,"fs":0.01353,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"0 P1P20 = 2(x2 - x1)2 + (y2 - y1)2 + (z2 - z1)2."},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.55445,"w":0.45917,"h":0.01602,"fs":0.01407,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"EXAMPLE 3 The distance between P1(2, 1, 5) and P2(-2, 3, 0) is"},{"x":0.46444,"y":0.56608,"w":0.30999,"h":0.02741,"fs":0.01353,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"0 P1P20 = 2(-2 - 2)2 + (3 - 1)2 + (0 - 5)2"},{"x":0.50893,"y":0.60151,"w":0.12367,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"= 216 + 4 + 25"},{"x":0.50893,"y":0.62453,"w":0.11962,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"= 245 ≈6.708."},{"x":0.11887,"y":0.65526,"w":0.06614,"h":0.01215,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"P0(x0, y0, z0)"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.66358,"w":0.59307,"h":0.02966,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"We can use the distance formula to write equations for spheres in space (Figure 12.6). A point P(x, y, z) lies on the sphere of radius a centered at P0(x0, y0, z0) precisely when"},{"x":0.1991,"y":0.66379,"w":0.04651,"h":0.01024,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"P(x, y, z)"},{"x":0.32659,"y":0.68118,"w":0.08468,"h":0.02741,"fs":0.01353,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"0 P0P0 = a or"},{"x":0.48258,"y":0.71981,"w":0.27042,"h":0.01947,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"(x - x0)2 + (y - y0)2 + (z - z0)2 = a2."},{"x":0.35359,"y":0.7731,"w":0.50481,"h":0.01445,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"The Standard Equation for the Sphere of Radius a and Center (x0, y0, z0)"},{"x":0.48462,"y":0.79112,"w":0.26635,"h":0.01947,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"(x - x0)2 + (y - y0)2 + (z - z0)2 = a2"},{"x":0.04849,"y":0.83163,"w":0.2347,"h":0.029,"fs":0.01151,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"FIGURE 12.6 The sphere of radius a centered at the point (x0, y0, z0)."},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.84836,"w":0.38023,"h":0.01449,"fs":0.01407,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"EXAMPLE 4 Find the center and radius of the sphere"},{"x":0.50057,"y":0.86792,"w":0.23487,"h":0.01795,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"x2 + y2 + z2 + 3x - 4z + 1 = 0."},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.90676,"w":0.59299,"h":0.02899,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"Solution We find the center and radius of a sphere the way we find the center and radius of a circle: Complete the squares on the x-, y-, and z-terms as necessary and write each"}]}